unim (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Modular Korean Input Method Engine written in Rust:
    - Core daemon (unim-daemon) with D-Bus session activation.
    - XIM and Wayland protocol servers (Wayland with
      zwp_input_popup_surface_v2 hanja/special-character popup).
    - C-API library (libunim_capi) and unified CLI tool (unim-cli,
      with a `config` subcommand for settings management).
    - GTK3 and GTK4 input method modules.
    - Qt5 and Qt6 platform input context plugins.
    - GTK4/libadwaita settings GUI (unim-gui-gtk).
    - Qt6/cxx-qt alternative GUI (unim-gui-qt).
    - im-config integration.
  * Supports 2-bul and 3-bul Hangul layouts, automatic Korean/English
    typo correction (TypeFix), Hanja conversion, special-character /
    emoji search and per-application input mode rules.
  * Nine binary packages let users pick the pieces they need:
    - unim-common  : core engine, daemon, CLI, shared library
    - unim-im-gtk  : GTK3 + GTK4 IM modules
    - unim-im-qt   : Qt5 + Qt6 platform input context plugins
    - unim-xim     : X11 XIM protocol frontend
    - unim-wayland : Wayland input-method frontend
    - unim-gui-gtk : GTK4/libadwaita settings GUI + tray
    - unim-gui-qt  : Qt6/cxx-qt settings GUI + tray (alternative)
    - unim-gnome   : GNOME Shell extension
    - unim         : meta-package pulling in everything

